          "body": "### Description\n\nCompare mode showed the ultra-processing level (NOVA group) image and label without any explanation of what the groups mean, so users had no way to interpret \"NOVA 4\" from the comparison itself.\n\nThis PR adds, next to the **Ultra-processing level** label in the comparison table:\n\n- an `InfoTooltip` with a concise explanation: *\"NOVA classifies foods by their degree of processing, from group 1 (unprocessed or minimally processed) to group 4 (ultra-processed). A lower group is generally better.\"*\n- a small \"Learn more\" external link (`target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"`, with `aria-label`/`title`) to https://world.openfoodfacts.org/nova\n\nBoth strings go through svelte-i18n (`compare.nova_group_info`, `compare.nova_group_learn_more`, added to `en-US.json` and `en.json`, with `default` fallbacks).\n\nTwo small supporting changes:\n\n- `InfoTooltip` gets an optional `position` prop (`top` | `bottom` | `left` | `right`, default `top` → existing usages unchanged). The help icon here sits at the left edge of the sticky first column, where the default top-centred tooltip was clipped by the viewport; it now opens to the right.\n- The label cell gets `hover:z-10 focus-within:z-10` so the open tooltip is not painted over by the sticky cells of the rows below.\n\nAcceptance criteria from the issue:\n- [x] Explanation is available from the Compare UI\n- [x] Tooltip text is concise and accessible (button with `aria-label`, keyboard focusable; DaisyUI tooltip shows on focus)\n- [x] Link to documentation provided\n\n### Screenshot or video\n\nVerified in the dev server on `/compare/shared?barcodes=3017620422003,737628064502` (Nutella vs. Thai Kitchen noodles): the label cell shows the help icon and external-link icon; hovering/focusing the help icon opens the tooltip to the right, fully readable and not clipped. Happy to attach a screenshot on request.\n\n### Related issue(s) and discussion\n\n- Fixes: #1658\n\n---\n\n### Checklist: Author Self-Review\n\n- [x] I have performed a self-review of my own code (including running it).\n- [x] I understand the changes I'm proposing and why they are needed.\n- [x] My changes generate no new warnings or errors (linting, console).\n- [x] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation (if applicable).\n\nPre-PR validation run locally: `pnpm format`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm check` (0 errors / 0 warnings), `pnpm test` (53 passed), `pnpm build` — all green.\n\n## Large Language Models usage disclosure\n\n- [ ] I did **not** use an LLM or AI tool to write this PR.\n- [x] I used an LLM / AI agent — details below:\n  - **Agent / tool name and version:** Claude Code (Claude Fable 5)\n  - **How it was used:** agentic (implemented, ran the validation commands and checked the result in the browser), under my account and review\n  - **I have reviewed and take full responsibility for all AI-generated code in this PR.**\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Added an informational tooltip to NOVA comparison details.\n  - Tooltips now support placement above, below, left, or right of associated content.\n  - Improved tooltip accessibility with descriptive labels and screen-reader support.\n- **Updates**\n  - Replaced the dedicated NOVA “Learn more” link with shared “More information” wording.\n  - Updated NOVA comparison text to remove the claim that lower groups are generally better.\n  - Removed the external NOVA documentation link from the comparison display.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
